1
00:01:38,985 --> 00:01:41,880
[Episode 23]

2
00:01:43,799 --> 00:01:45,600
Xing Wu.

3
00:01:49,439 --> 00:01:51,760
Are you sure you're okay?

4
00:01:57,280 --> 00:01:58,439
I'm good.

5
00:01:58,439 --> 00:02:00,239
What's there to worry about?

6
00:02:00,239 --> 00:02:02,079
I'll just grab some popsicles

7
00:02:02,079 --> 00:02:03,680
from the fridge.

8
00:02:03,680 --> 00:02:05,520
Just ice it, and it'll be okay.

9
00:02:05,520 --> 00:02:07,480
I can even eat them afterward.

10
00:02:21,038 --> 00:02:22,879
Then I'll go check on Grandma

11
00:02:22,879 --> 00:02:25,200
to see if they need anything.

12
00:02:30,199 --> 00:02:31,720
Good night.

13
00:02:56,400 --> 00:02:57,520
Grandma.

14
00:02:57,520 --> 00:02:59,439
I've changed the bedding for you.

15
00:02:59,439 --> 00:03:01,360
I also put an electric blanket on for you.

16
00:03:01,360 --> 00:03:02,919
Turn it on if you feel cold.

17
00:03:02,919 --> 00:03:05,199
I've set the air conditioner for you too.

18
00:03:05,199 --> 00:03:06,520
If you feel too warm,

19
00:03:06,520 --> 00:03:08,360
just turn it down.

20
00:03:08,360 --> 00:03:09,441
The remote control

21
00:03:09,441 --> 00:03:11,640
is on the right side of the nightstand.

22
00:03:12,398 --> 00:03:14,719
Thank you. Thank you so much.

23
00:03:14,719 --> 00:03:16,760
- Don't mention it.
- Really, thank you.

24
00:03:19,280 --> 00:03:21,240
Grandma, I brought you

25
00:03:21,240 --> 00:03:23,966
some slippers and pajamas.

26
00:03:23,966 --> 00:03:26,166
They're brand new and have never been worn.

27
00:03:26,166 --> 00:03:28,240
My size. They'll fit for sure.

28
00:03:28,240 --> 00:03:30,040
Let me help you put them on.

29
00:03:30,040 --> 00:03:31,840
No, it's okay. No need.

30
00:03:31,840 --> 00:03:33,481
- It's fine.
- Let Lan Fang help me.

31
00:03:33,481 --> 00:03:35,480
Just let Lan Fang help me.

32
00:03:36,199 --> 00:03:37,760
Fen.

33
00:03:39,159 --> 00:03:40,759
Let me do it.

34
00:03:40,759 --> 00:03:42,560
Thank you.

35
00:03:42,560 --> 00:03:44,039
Alright then. Fang, then you

36
00:03:44,039 --> 00:03:45,240
help Grandma change.

37
00:03:45,240 --> 00:03:47,919
I'll go get some more toiletries.

38
00:03:47,919 --> 00:03:49,240
And I'll go

39
00:03:49,240 --> 00:03:51,120
boil some water.

40
00:04:03,680 --> 00:04:05,400
Come, put your arm around me.

41
00:04:09,560 --> 00:04:11,040
All done.

42
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:18,439
Are you cold?

43
00:04:18,439 --> 00:04:20,000
No.

44
00:04:25,399 --> 00:04:26,840
Okay.

45
00:04:51,920 --> 00:04:53,639
Lan Fang...

46
00:04:53,639 --> 00:04:55,360
I-I didn't do it

47
00:04:55,360 --> 00:04:57,439
on purpose.

48
00:04:57,439 --> 00:04:59,279
I know.

49
00:04:59,279 --> 00:05:02,160
I know you didn't mean it.

50
00:05:03,072 --> 00:05:04,160
No,

51
00:05:04,160 --> 00:05:06,439
my legs just went numb.

52
00:05:06,439 --> 00:05:08,120
I don't know how it happened.

53
00:05:08,120 --> 00:05:10,320
But it just did.

54
00:05:15,639 --> 00:05:17,399
You stubborn old woman.

55
00:05:17,399 --> 00:05:19,800
You seem so happy all the time,

56
00:05:19,800 --> 00:05:22,040
but you're just as stubborn as Xing Wu.

57
00:05:22,040 --> 00:05:23,519
A stubborn mule.

58
00:05:23,519 --> 00:05:25,040
You love to just suffer in silence.

59
00:05:25,040 --> 00:05:26,360
You never say anything.

60
00:05:26,360 --> 00:05:28,440
You don't say a word even when asked.

61
00:05:28,440 --> 00:05:29,960
- No...
- You all love to hold it all in.

62
00:05:29,960 --> 00:05:32,199
Aren't you tired?

63
00:05:32,199 --> 00:05:33,839
You should learn from me.

64
00:05:33,839 --> 00:05:35,079
Eat when you're hungry.

65
00:05:35,079 --> 00:05:37,199
Sleep when you're tired.

66
00:05:37,199 --> 00:05:39,080
When life throws

67
00:05:39,720 --> 00:05:41,160
hardship and trouble at you,

68
00:05:41,160 --> 00:05:42,880
just accept them.

69
00:05:44,133 --> 00:05:46,240
I understand.

70
00:05:57,560 --> 00:05:58,600
Lan Fang.

71
00:05:58,600 --> 00:05:59,639
I...

72
00:05:59,639 --> 00:06:00,920
Don't get mad.

73
00:06:00,920 --> 00:06:02,760
Don't get mad.

74
00:06:06,800 --> 00:06:08,879
I'm not blaming you.

75
00:06:08,879 --> 00:06:11,400
And I'm not scolding you.

76
00:06:12,305 --> 00:06:15,240
I just feel bad for you.

77
00:06:15,240 --> 00:06:18,567
I'm scared you'll get sick
if you keep everything inside.

78
00:06:18,567 --> 00:06:20,880
You know what I mean?

79
00:06:21,480 --> 00:06:23,480
I know.

80
00:06:28,140 --> 00:06:30,279
But Lan Fang...

81
00:06:30,279 --> 00:06:31,959
We've just been so unlucky.

82
00:06:31,959 --> 00:06:34,560
What are we going to do now?

83
00:06:34,560 --> 00:06:37,240
So what if Xuan Island is gone?

84
00:06:37,240 --> 00:06:39,680
I'm not going to abandon you.

85
00:06:40,720 --> 00:06:43,199
I'll never leave you.

86
00:06:43,199 --> 00:06:45,160
I know.

87
00:06:45,920 --> 00:06:48,480
All my life, it's been you and Wu

88
00:06:48,480 --> 00:06:50,319
looking after me.

89
00:06:50,319 --> 00:06:52,760
I'm your daughter-in-law.

90
00:06:53,959 --> 00:06:56,560
My son was a failure.

91
00:06:56,560 --> 00:06:59,000
But I'm so lucky to have you.

92
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:02,600
You're just like my own daughter.

93
00:07:02,600 --> 00:07:05,079
I've been fortunate.

94
00:07:05,079 --> 00:07:06,800
If it weren't for you and Wu,

95
00:07:06,800 --> 00:07:08,440
I'm afraid

96
00:07:08,440 --> 00:07:09,493
I'd be dead

97
00:07:09,493 --> 00:07:12,160
by now.

98
00:07:18,800 --> 00:07:20,650
Stop crying.

99
00:07:20,650 --> 00:07:22,920
Don't cry anymore.

100
00:07:25,600 --> 00:07:28,120
We'll get through this.

101
00:07:28,120 --> 00:07:29,959
We'll definitely be fine.

102
00:07:29,959 --> 00:07:32,520
It's going to be okay.

103
00:07:33,879 --> 00:07:35,361
Lan Fang,

104
00:07:35,361 --> 00:07:37,480
I...

105
00:07:38,759 --> 00:07:40,319
Look,

106
00:07:40,319 --> 00:07:42,519
I got this out

107
00:07:42,519 --> 00:07:45,040
when the fire was going.

108
00:07:45,040 --> 00:07:47,160
I'm not a useless old woman.

109
00:07:47,160 --> 00:07:48,199
See?

110
00:07:48,199 --> 00:07:51,230
There's quite a bit of money in this.

111
00:07:56,439 --> 00:07:58,000
Mom.

112
00:08:49,565 --> 00:08:52,200
- Wu.
<i>- Hello, Mom.</i>

113
00:08:52,200 --> 00:08:53,360
<i>How's everything over there?</i>

114
00:08:53,360 --> 00:08:54,679
I'm good.

115
00:08:54,679 --> 00:08:56,200
Grandma just went to sleep.

116
00:08:56,200 --> 00:08:57,880
That's good.

117
00:09:00,498 --> 00:09:02,578
What about you?

118
00:09:02,578 --> 00:09:04,080
Are you okay?

119
00:09:04,080 --> 00:09:06,279
I'm fine.

120
00:09:06,279 --> 00:09:08,400
Don't you know me?

121
00:09:08,400 --> 00:09:10,881
You don't need to worry about me.

122
00:09:11,719 --> 00:09:14,240
I wanted to get some things for Grandma,

123
00:09:14,240 --> 00:09:15,919
but all the shops were closed.

124
00:09:15,919 --> 00:09:17,240
<i>You don't need to buy anything.</i>

125
00:09:17,240 --> 00:09:19,039
Auntie Jin has already prepared

126
00:09:19,039 --> 00:09:21,440
all the daily necessities for Grandma and me.

127
00:09:22,039 --> 00:09:23,671
Alright, good.

128
00:09:25,625 --> 00:09:27,485
I'll come over to see Grandma tomorrow.

129
00:09:27,485 --> 00:09:29,720
Okay. Come back tomorrow.

130
00:09:29,720 --> 00:09:31,840
Get some good rest today.

131
00:09:31,840 --> 00:09:33,400
You too.

132
00:10:05,032 --> 00:10:06,279
Fang.

133
00:10:06,279 --> 00:10:08,120
You must be worn out.

134
00:10:08,120 --> 00:10:09,679
I made you some dumplings.

135
00:10:09,679 --> 00:10:12,200
- Eat them while they're hot.
- I'm not hungry.

136
00:10:12,200 --> 00:10:13,440
Just have a little.

137
00:10:13,440 --> 00:10:15,720
I just can't eat.

138
00:10:16,959 --> 00:10:18,320
You came too.

139
00:10:18,320 --> 00:10:20,360
- Same thought.
- Same thought.

140
00:10:21,240 --> 00:10:23,040
Eat something.

141
00:10:26,919 --> 00:10:28,639
If you're feeling upset,

142
00:10:28,639 --> 00:10:31,080
just talk to us.

143
00:10:31,080 --> 00:10:32,799
If you don't want to talk,

144
00:10:32,799 --> 00:10:34,080
at least take a few bites.

145
00:10:34,080 --> 00:10:35,680
Yes, have some.

146
00:10:38,919 --> 00:10:41,320
I've been thinking...

147
00:10:41,320 --> 00:10:44,440
Inside my cash drawer,
there was a few thousand yuan.

148
00:10:44,440 --> 00:10:47,720
I planned to spend it
on visiting relatives for the New Year.

149
00:10:47,720 --> 00:10:50,120
Why on earth didn't I

150
00:10:50,120 --> 00:10:52,759
think to withdraw it earlier?

151
00:10:52,759 --> 00:10:54,840
Who could've seen this coming?

152
00:10:54,840 --> 00:10:56,279
It's not your fault.

153
00:10:56,279 --> 00:10:57,679
Stop blaming yourself.

154
00:10:57,679 --> 00:10:59,879
Who else is there to blame?

155
00:10:59,879 --> 00:11:01,440
Now Ye's textbooks are gone,

156
00:11:01,440 --> 00:11:04,080
and Wu's review materials are lost too.

157
00:11:05,385 --> 00:11:07,200
If they can't get into college

158
00:11:07,200 --> 00:11:08,840
because of this fire,

159
00:11:08,840 --> 00:11:10,399
it's all my fault.

160
00:11:10,399 --> 00:11:11,801
I would've destroyed

161
00:11:11,801 --> 00:11:14,080
their bright futures.

162
00:11:14,919 --> 00:11:16,639
You can buy them new books.

163
00:11:16,639 --> 00:11:18,960
They can do the exercises again.

164
00:11:18,960 --> 00:11:21,679
As long as you're all safe,

165
00:11:21,679 --> 00:11:24,559
you can start over from scratch.

166
00:11:24,559 --> 00:11:26,080
Tell me, why does this

167
00:11:26,080 --> 00:11:27,879
keep happening to me?

168
00:11:27,879 --> 00:11:30,840
Right when things get a little better,
trouble knocks on my door again.

169
00:11:30,840 --> 00:11:33,760
Every single time. What did I do wrong?

170
00:11:33,760 --> 00:11:35,399
But you've made it through every time.

171
00:11:35,399 --> 00:11:37,480
We're doing okay, aren't we?

172
00:11:37,480 --> 00:11:40,039
What's done is done.

173
00:11:40,039 --> 00:11:43,039
But now, my home is gone.

174
00:11:43,039 --> 00:11:46,440
From now on, my home is yours.

175
00:11:46,440 --> 00:11:48,279
As long as I have something to eat and drink,

176
00:11:48,279 --> 00:11:51,519
I won't let my best friend end up homeless.

177
00:11:51,519 --> 00:11:54,440
I mean it.

178
00:11:54,440 --> 00:11:57,120
Exactly. If you need money,

179
00:11:57,120 --> 00:11:58,720
just come to me.

180
00:11:58,720 --> 00:12:01,080
Now is exactly when you need us the most.

181
00:12:01,080 --> 00:12:03,000
- And we've got your back.
- Yes.

182
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:04,519
Here, take this money for now.

183
00:12:04,519 --> 00:12:06,400
I've got some too.

184
00:12:07,240 --> 00:12:09,519
- Same again.
- Same again.

185
00:12:09,519 --> 00:12:11,600
- Take it.
- Go on, take it.

186
00:12:14,278 --> 00:12:16,119
Alright, stop crying.

187
00:12:17,720 --> 00:12:18,800
How did I,

188
00:12:18,800 --> 00:12:22,240
Li Lan Fang, get so lucky

189
00:12:22,240 --> 00:12:25,348
to have friends like you?

190
00:12:25,348 --> 00:12:28,120
Well, we're all women.

191
00:12:28,120 --> 00:12:29,714
Girls help girls.

192
00:12:29,714 --> 00:12:32,120
Wait, whose dog died?

193
00:12:32,726 --> 00:12:35,080
It's New Year's. Why bring up death?

194
00:12:35,080 --> 00:12:36,240
"Girls"

195
00:12:36,240 --> 00:12:38,120
means women.

196
00:12:38,120 --> 00:12:39,360
"help girls" means...

197
00:12:39,360 --> 00:12:42,640
women shouldn't make it hard for each other.

198
00:12:46,919 --> 00:12:48,960
Come on, have some.

199
00:12:54,240 --> 00:12:55,240
Take it slow.

200
00:12:55,240 --> 00:12:57,840
- Who made the better ones?
- Both are good.

201
00:12:59,039 --> 00:13:01,360
Okay, no more tears.

202
00:13:24,960 --> 00:13:27,039
<i>Wu, I've got the wheelchair.</i>

203
00:13:27,039 --> 00:13:29,360
<i>I'll take it to your grandma.</i>

204
00:13:34,679 --> 00:13:37,360
<i>Textbooks, notes, and review materials...</i>

205
00:13:37,360 --> 00:13:39,320
<i>I've got them all sorted.</i>

206
00:13:39,320 --> 00:13:40,679
<i>I'll go to my dad's office tomorrow</i>

207
00:13:40,679 --> 00:13:42,600
<i>- and make two copies of everything.</i>
- Thank you.

208
00:13:42,600 --> 00:13:44,080
<i>Xing Wu,</i>

209
00:13:44,080 --> 00:13:45,960
<i>stay strong.</i>

210
00:13:45,960 --> 00:13:47,800
<i>And Qing Ye too.</i>

211
00:14:15,809 --> 00:14:18,933
[Xuan Island Barbershop]

212
00:15:18,960 --> 00:15:21,159
<i>Three, two, one.</i>

213
00:15:21,159 --> 00:15:23,600
<i>- Cheese!
- Cheese!</i>

214
00:15:51,840 --> 00:15:54,200
<i>- Happy New Year!
- Happy New Year!</i>

215
00:18:35,319 --> 00:18:37,680
Xing Wu.

216
00:18:37,680 --> 00:18:40,007
Don't be sad.

217
00:18:40,007 --> 00:18:42,640
Everything will pass.

218
00:18:42,640 --> 00:18:45,120
Things will get better.

219
00:19:26,160 --> 00:19:28,120
Why did you come?

220
00:19:30,519 --> 00:19:32,160
I woke up this morning

221
00:19:32,160 --> 00:19:34,079
and didn't see you.

222
00:19:34,079 --> 00:19:35,359
I thought

223
00:19:35,359 --> 00:19:37,079
you would be here.

224
00:19:37,079 --> 00:19:39,160
Besides,

225
00:19:39,160 --> 00:19:40,720
I came over

226
00:19:40,720 --> 00:19:43,720
to look for your New Year's gift.

227
00:19:45,919 --> 00:19:48,200
What kind of gift?

228
00:19:48,200 --> 00:19:49,759
A keychain.

229
00:19:49,759 --> 00:19:52,440
I put it under your pillow.

230
00:19:52,440 --> 00:19:54,000
I was hoping that

231
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:57,119
when you woke up this morning,

232
00:19:57,119 --> 00:19:58,960
you would see it.

233
00:20:00,480 --> 00:20:02,000
Xing Wu.

234
00:20:13,359 --> 00:20:15,240
Did you find it?

235
00:20:17,799 --> 00:20:18,880
This one?

236
00:20:18,880 --> 00:20:20,560
Yes.

237
00:20:21,880 --> 00:20:24,039
How did it get burned like that?

238
00:20:24,039 --> 00:20:26,079
I should have given it to you earlier.

239
00:20:26,079 --> 00:20:28,200
It's okay. I like it.

240
00:20:28,200 --> 00:20:29,839
It looks vintage.

241
00:20:29,839 --> 00:20:31,760
It suits me perfectly.

242
00:20:35,175 --> 00:20:36,675
I just took a quick look at Xuan Island.

243
00:20:36,675 --> 00:20:38,160
There's still plenty of good stuff left.

244
00:20:38,160 --> 00:20:41,119
I'll call Li Lan Fang and tell her about it.

245
00:20:41,119 --> 00:20:42,200
That's great.

246
00:20:42,200 --> 00:20:44,039
So Auntie and Grandma don't have to worry.

247
00:20:44,039 --> 00:20:46,440
There's still hope for Xuan Island.

248
00:20:46,440 --> 00:20:48,039
I also borrowed a wheelchair.

249
00:20:48,039 --> 00:20:50,240
It's mainly for Grandma.

250
00:20:53,319 --> 00:20:55,359
Look, that's just...

251
00:20:55,359 --> 00:20:56,720
how life is.

252
00:20:56,720 --> 00:20:58,720
Like it's making fun of me.

253
00:21:02,920 --> 00:21:05,880
Have you seen Forrest Gump?

254
00:21:05,880 --> 00:21:07,960
In that movie, it says

255
00:21:07,960 --> 00:21:10,800
"Life is like a box of chocolates.

256
00:21:10,800 --> 00:21:14,080
You never know what you're going to get."

257
00:21:16,559 --> 00:21:18,120
I think...

258
00:21:18,120 --> 00:21:20,240
mine is bitter right now.

259
00:21:20,240 --> 00:21:21,799
But the next one

260
00:21:21,799 --> 00:21:23,920
should be sweet.

261
00:21:31,559 --> 00:21:33,669
- Can I have a taste?
- Yes.

262
00:21:37,206 --> 00:21:38,799
Xing Wu,

263
00:21:38,799 --> 00:21:41,120
I believe that someday,

264
00:21:41,759 --> 00:21:44,040
we'll have everything we want.

265
00:21:46,633 --> 00:21:48,520
I think so too.

266
00:21:58,359 --> 00:22:00,839
We will definitely rebuild

267
00:22:00,839 --> 00:22:03,119
a better home.

268
00:22:03,119 --> 00:22:04,840
It will definitely be

269
00:22:04,840 --> 00:22:06,640
even cozier.

270
00:22:06,640 --> 00:22:07,720
Of course.

271
00:22:07,720 --> 00:22:10,119
And your room should be redesigned too.

272
00:22:10,119 --> 00:22:11,519
Where should we put the family photo?

273
00:22:11,519 --> 00:22:13,812
In the bedrooms. Just hang one in each.

274
00:22:13,812 --> 00:22:15,560
As for your wardrobe and mirror,

275
00:22:15,560 --> 00:22:19,120
I'll have a bigger set custom-made for you.

276
00:22:19,960 --> 00:22:22,240
Don't forget the air conditioner.

277
00:22:22,240 --> 00:22:24,920
No second-hand ones this time.
I'll buy brand new ones.

278
00:22:24,920 --> 00:22:26,800
Grandma's room needs one too.

279
00:22:26,800 --> 00:22:27,840
Of course.

280
00:22:27,840 --> 00:22:29,359
And for Li Lan Fang, we'll get her

281
00:22:29,359 --> 00:22:30,720
a whole new set of salon gear.

282
00:22:30,720 --> 00:22:31,720
Exactly.

283
00:22:31,720 --> 00:22:33,634
We need more shampoo chairs.

284
00:22:33,634 --> 00:22:34,920
That'll make the business better.

285
00:22:34,920 --> 00:22:37,200
We're on the same page.

286
00:22:41,039 --> 00:22:42,759
But...

287
00:22:42,759 --> 00:22:44,920
rebuilding our home

288
00:22:45,720 --> 00:22:48,462
will cost a lot, right?

289
00:22:55,079 --> 00:22:56,560
Yes.

290
00:23:02,960 --> 00:23:04,600
But it's okay.

291
00:23:06,279 --> 00:23:07,880
So, this time,

292
00:23:07,880 --> 00:23:10,039
will you leave school

293
00:23:10,039 --> 00:23:11,960
to make money for the family?

294
00:23:15,200 --> 00:23:16,920
This time,

295
00:23:17,640 --> 00:23:19,519
I'm not giving up.

296
00:23:19,519 --> 00:23:21,680
Making money and studying...

297
00:23:22,519 --> 00:23:24,280
I want both.

298
00:24:30,799 --> 00:24:32,393
Wu.

299
00:24:32,393 --> 00:24:34,200
Did you go to Xuan Island early this morning?

300
00:24:34,200 --> 00:24:35,686
Yes.

301
00:24:37,599 --> 00:24:39,279
Don't you think the fire at your place

302
00:24:39,279 --> 00:24:40,839
was a little suspicious?

303
00:24:40,839 --> 00:24:42,839
Let the police figure that out.

304
00:24:42,839 --> 00:24:44,280
A fire on New Year's?

305
00:24:44,280 --> 00:24:46,720
Someone must have set it.

306
00:24:48,000 --> 00:24:49,559
Anyway, Hu and I

307
00:24:49,559 --> 00:24:51,759
both think something is off.

308
00:24:51,759 --> 00:24:53,519
When Cao Ping and Yang Gang

309
00:24:53,519 --> 00:24:55,039
got taken to the police station,

310
00:24:55,039 --> 00:24:57,720
I was worried he would get back at you.

311
00:24:57,720 --> 00:25:00,650
Even though Cao Fan helped you out that time,

312
00:25:00,650 --> 00:25:04,200
I think someone like him...

313
00:25:04,200 --> 00:25:06,560
could do anything.

314
00:25:16,637 --> 00:25:18,960
Hey, Xing Wu, what are you doing?

315
00:25:20,511 --> 00:25:22,759
- What are you doing?
- Did you set the fire?

316
00:25:22,759 --> 00:25:23,960
What fire?

317
00:25:23,960 --> 00:25:25,319
My house caught fire last night.

318
00:25:25,319 --> 00:25:26,940
- Did you do it?
- Your house caught fire?

319
00:25:26,940 --> 00:25:29,395
What does that have to do with me?

320
00:25:32,279 --> 00:25:34,680
Then why do you have gas at home?

321
00:25:34,680 --> 00:25:36,519
So what if I have gas at home?

322
00:25:36,519 --> 00:25:38,880
If I did it, would I be here waiting for you?

323
00:25:38,880 --> 00:25:40,943
You'd better tell the truth.

324
00:25:40,943 --> 00:25:42,920
I've called the police.

325
00:25:44,552 --> 00:25:46,880
Let go. Let go!

326
00:25:51,400 --> 00:25:53,840
<i>I don't care what happens to me,</i>

327
00:25:54,519 --> 00:25:57,280
<i>but I can't mess up my sister's life again.</i>

328
00:26:12,814 --> 00:26:14,600
Take it or leave it.

329
00:26:32,160 --> 00:26:33,319
Hello?

330
00:26:33,319 --> 00:26:34,452
<i>Xing Wu.</i>

331
00:26:34,452 --> 00:26:36,160
<i>Officer Xu is at the house.</i>

332
00:26:36,160 --> 00:26:37,960
<i>He wants you to go to the station.</i>

333
00:26:37,960 --> 00:26:39,839
<i>They're looking into the cause of the fire.</i>

334
00:26:39,839 --> 00:26:42,119
<i>They're gathering clues and evidence.</i>

335
00:26:42,119 --> 00:26:43,559
<i>You think Cao Ping did it?</i>

336
00:26:43,559 --> 00:26:45,680
I'm with him right now.

337
00:26:45,680 --> 00:26:47,279
I don't think it was him.

338
00:26:47,279 --> 00:26:49,640
Wait for me. I'll be right back.

339
00:26:54,000 --> 00:26:57,200
The cause of the fire has been found.

340
00:26:57,200 --> 00:26:58,680
Look.

341
00:27:00,519 --> 00:27:01,599
Yang Gang.

342
00:27:01,599 --> 00:27:03,880
Yes. According to our investigation,

343
00:27:03,880 --> 00:27:05,200
before the fire happened,

344
00:27:05,200 --> 00:27:08,827
neighbors saw him there.

345
00:27:31,759 --> 00:27:34,000
He dropped a cigarette butt at the scene,

346
00:27:34,000 --> 00:27:36,000
and it lit some cardboard in the backyard.

347
00:27:36,000 --> 00:27:38,360
Then the wind fanned it into a fire.

348
00:27:50,536 --> 00:27:51,880
He is suspected of negligent arson.

349
00:27:51,880 --> 00:27:55,160
He's under criminal detention as per the law.

350
00:27:59,640 --> 00:28:01,279
Officer...

351
00:28:01,279 --> 00:28:03,280
I didn't do it on purpose.

352
00:28:03,280 --> 00:28:05,079
It's not a crime if it's an accident, right?

353
00:28:05,079 --> 00:28:06,519
We've fully investigated

354
00:28:06,519 --> 00:28:08,519
the cause of the fire.

355
00:28:08,519 --> 00:28:12,079
It was caused by a cigarette butt
that you carelessly left at the scene.

356
00:28:12,079 --> 00:28:13,240
Your actions

357
00:28:13,240 --> 00:28:15,200
have endangered public safety.

358
00:28:15,200 --> 00:28:17,079
This is the crime of negligent arson.

359
00:28:17,079 --> 00:28:18,491
According to the law,

360
00:28:18,491 --> 00:28:20,560
if the damage is minor,

361
00:28:20,560 --> 00:28:22,920
you will face up to three years in prison

362
00:28:22,920 --> 00:28:24,079
or criminal detention.

363
00:28:24,079 --> 00:28:25,519
If the damage is serious,

364
00:28:25,519 --> 00:28:28,680
you will face three to seven years in prison.

365
00:28:28,680 --> 00:28:30,279
I just threw a cigarette butt.

366
00:28:30,279 --> 00:28:31,960
I never expected it to be this bad.

367
00:28:31,960 --> 00:28:34,000
You have the right to get a lawyer.

368
00:28:34,000 --> 00:28:35,440
But there's something else

369
00:28:35,440 --> 00:28:36,920
I have to tell you.

370
00:28:36,920 --> 00:28:38,160
What? What is it?

371
00:28:38,160 --> 00:28:40,073
You're suspected of illegal business.

372
00:28:40,073 --> 00:28:42,759
We have already seized your warehouse by law.

373
00:28:42,759 --> 00:28:43,759
We found that

374
00:28:43,759 --> 00:28:47,000
most of the items in your warehouse are stolen.

375
00:28:47,000 --> 00:28:48,559
Those aren't stolen.

376
00:28:48,559 --> 00:28:49,725
They're just refurbished.

377
00:28:49,725 --> 00:28:52,120
If you can't provide a reasonable explanation

378
00:28:52,120 --> 00:28:54,920
for where these items came from,

379
00:28:54,920 --> 00:28:56,401
we will transfer the case

380
00:28:56,401 --> 00:28:58,605
to the prosecutor for prosecution.

381
00:28:58,605 --> 00:28:59,846
So,

382
00:28:59,846 --> 00:29:01,720
please cooperate with our investigation

383
00:29:01,720 --> 00:29:04,560
and explain everything clearly.

384
00:29:06,079 --> 00:29:07,680
Okay. Thank you.

385
00:29:07,680 --> 00:29:08,960
No problem.

386
00:29:08,960 --> 00:29:11,000
That's the current situation of the case.

387
00:29:11,000 --> 00:29:12,119
You can go home for now.

388
00:29:12,119 --> 00:29:13,160
If anything else comes up,

389
00:29:13,160 --> 00:29:15,285
I'll call you.

390
00:29:15,285 --> 00:29:17,723
Wu, take good care of your grandma.

391
00:29:17,723 --> 00:29:19,061
- Thanks, Officer Xu.
- It's okay.

392
00:29:19,061 --> 00:29:20,200
- Sorry for the trouble.
- I'll get back to work now.

393
00:29:20,200 --> 00:29:22,160
- Alright. Thank you.
- Goodbye.

394
00:29:23,960 --> 00:29:25,559
Officer Xu just said that

395
00:29:25,559 --> 00:29:27,519
Yang Gang doesn't own any property.

396
00:29:27,519 --> 00:29:30,280
So for now, we won't get any compensation.

397
00:29:30,880 --> 00:29:33,720
We can only rely on ourselves.

398
00:29:33,720 --> 00:29:36,960
We cleared all our debts before the New Year.

399
00:29:36,960 --> 00:29:38,240
And now,

400
00:29:38,240 --> 00:29:40,039
we have to get back into debt.

401
00:29:40,039 --> 00:29:41,559
Don't worry, Mom.

402
00:29:41,559 --> 00:29:44,120
Let's just pretend we're starting from nothing

403
00:29:44,120 --> 00:29:46,223
and building it all over again.

404
00:29:47,400 --> 00:29:49,759
But that will be so tough on you.

405
00:29:49,759 --> 00:29:51,401
- No, it won't.
- Grandma.

406
00:29:51,401 --> 00:29:52,799
After every storm comes a rainbow.

407
00:29:52,799 --> 00:29:53,799
We will definitely

408
00:29:53,799 --> 00:29:56,440
do our best to get through this.

409
00:29:56,440 --> 00:29:57,440
Grandma,

410
00:29:57,440 --> 00:29:58,800
I'll work even harder.

411
00:29:58,800 --> 00:30:00,519
Things will get better and better.

412
00:30:00,519 --> 00:30:02,080
Trust me.

413
00:30:02,798 --> 00:30:04,200
It's New Year's.

414
00:30:04,200 --> 00:30:06,000
The luckiest thing is that our whole family

415
00:30:06,000 --> 00:30:07,720
is together and safe.

416
00:30:07,720 --> 00:30:09,200
So we should smile.

417
00:30:09,200 --> 00:30:10,519
Come on, smile.

418
00:30:10,519 --> 00:30:12,160
Smile.

419
00:30:12,160 --> 00:30:13,559
Smile.

420
00:30:13,559 --> 00:30:15,400
Come on, let's go home.

421
00:30:23,360 --> 00:30:26,121
Why is it so lively over there?
Is there some kind of event going on?

422
00:30:26,121 --> 00:30:28,400
Maybe they're praying to
the Dragon King and Mazu.

423
00:30:28,400 --> 00:30:31,080
Let's go pray too.

424
00:30:47,079 --> 00:30:48,160
We coastal people

425
00:30:48,160 --> 00:30:49,961
believe in the Dragon King and Mazu.

426
00:30:49,961 --> 00:30:51,320
All of us

427
00:30:51,320 --> 00:30:53,240
should make a wish too.

428
00:30:53,240 --> 00:30:55,160
I hope Mazu will bless us

429
00:30:55,160 --> 00:30:56,519
and keep our family safe.

430
00:30:56,519 --> 00:30:59,080
May everything go well.

431
00:30:59,920 --> 00:31:01,920
May Mazu bless

432
00:31:01,920 --> 00:31:03,200
Wu and Ye

433
00:31:03,200 --> 00:31:04,440
so they can get into

434
00:31:04,440 --> 00:31:06,720
the colleges they want.

435
00:31:08,067 --> 00:31:10,759
May Grandma stay healthy.

436
00:31:10,759 --> 00:31:13,400
May Qing Ye get into her dream university.

437
00:31:13,400 --> 00:31:15,160
Please bless Mom

438
00:31:15,160 --> 00:31:16,840
to make a lot of money.

439
00:31:20,000 --> 00:31:21,240
<i>I hope</i>

440
00:31:21,240 --> 00:31:23,805
<i>we can always be a family.</i>

441
00:31:23,805 --> 00:31:25,240
<i>Xing Wu and I</i>

442
00:31:25,240 --> 00:31:27,093
<i>will always be together.</i>

443
00:31:29,519 --> 00:31:32,079
What about you? What did you pray for?

444
00:31:32,079 --> 00:31:33,440
I'm not telling you.

445
00:31:33,440 --> 00:31:34,519
Say it out loud.

446
00:31:34,519 --> 00:31:35,640
It won't come true otherwise.

447
00:31:35,640 --> 00:31:37,039
You're lying.

448
00:31:37,039 --> 00:31:39,320
It'll come true either way.

449
00:31:52,680 --> 00:31:55,021
<i>Hawthorns are very sour.</i>

450
00:31:55,021 --> 00:31:57,200
<i>But when you coat them in sugar,</i>

451
00:31:57,200 --> 00:32:00,067
<i>they turn into a New Year's treat.</i>

452
00:32:00,067 --> 00:32:02,240
<i>Life is like that too, isn't it?</i>

453
00:32:02,240 --> 00:32:05,519
<i>Wrapping bitter days in a sugar coating</i>

454
00:32:05,519 --> 00:32:07,810
<i>makes them memorable.</i>

455
00:32:13,279 --> 00:32:14,599
I'm going now. Take care.

456
00:32:14,599 --> 00:32:16,320
Sorry for the trouble again.

457
00:32:16,320 --> 00:32:18,079
It's no trouble at all.

458
00:32:18,079 --> 00:32:19,079
Thank you, Auntie.

459
00:32:19,079 --> 00:32:20,839
We won't be staying too long.

460
00:32:20,839 --> 00:32:23,960
Yeah. We plan to rent a place

461
00:32:23,960 --> 00:32:25,119
after the Lantern Festival.

462
00:32:25,119 --> 00:32:26,160
Why rent a place?

463
00:32:26,160 --> 00:32:28,519
I told you, my home is your home.

464
00:32:28,519 --> 00:32:30,261
You can stay as long as you need.

465
00:32:30,261 --> 00:32:31,599
If you need anything, just say it.

466
00:32:31,599 --> 00:32:33,465
Good to have you.

467
00:32:33,465 --> 00:32:35,039
By the way,

468
00:32:35,039 --> 00:32:36,400
keep the house keys.

469
00:32:36,400 --> 00:32:38,200
- Okay.
- I'll get extras if you need.

470
00:32:38,200 --> 00:32:40,519
It's enough. That's plenty.

471
00:32:40,519 --> 00:32:41,935
I'm leaving now. Goodbye.

472
00:32:41,935 --> 00:32:43,624
- Message me if you need.
- Sure. Bye, Auntie.

473
00:32:43,624 --> 00:32:45,448
Take care.

474
00:32:45,448 --> 00:32:47,200
- Wu.
- Thank you, Auntie Jin.

475
00:32:47,200 --> 00:32:48,520
Don't mention it.

476
00:32:48,520 --> 00:32:50,356
- Sorry for the trouble.
- Tell me if you need anything, bye.

477
00:32:50,356 --> 00:32:53,000
We will stay in Xi Xi's room.

478
00:32:53,000 --> 00:32:56,039
Ye can stay in Hu's room.

479
00:32:56,039 --> 00:32:57,600
What about Xing Wu?

480
00:32:57,600 --> 00:32:59,360
I'll sleep in the living room.

481
00:33:00,519 --> 00:33:02,005
What's all this?

482
00:33:02,005 --> 00:33:04,395
Everyone gathered some clothes
and daily necessities for us.

483
00:33:04,395 --> 00:33:06,827
They got some for you and Grandma.
New Year's stuff is pricey.

484
00:33:06,827 --> 00:33:08,553
- So they just pooled what they could.
- Okay.

485
00:33:08,553 --> 00:33:10,266
- I'll take them inside.
- Okay.

486
00:33:10,266 --> 00:33:13,160
Lan Fang, didn't I give you the card?

487
00:33:13,160 --> 00:33:15,640
Just go ahead and use it.

488
00:33:15,640 --> 00:33:16,880
As the old saying goes,

489
00:33:16,880 --> 00:33:18,000
when you're past 50,

490
00:33:18,000 --> 00:33:19,559
you shouldn't touch your savings.

491
00:33:19,559 --> 00:33:20,640
That money is for you

492
00:33:20,640 --> 00:33:22,160
to live on.

493
00:33:22,160 --> 00:33:24,400
Now is exactly the time to use it.

494
00:33:24,400 --> 00:33:26,920
We need food and clothes right now.

495
00:33:26,920 --> 00:33:28,640
It's just right for this crisis.

496
00:33:28,640 --> 00:33:30,600
Let's use it. Don't worry.

497
00:33:30,600 --> 00:33:32,079
When I make big money someday,

498
00:33:32,079 --> 00:33:35,200
I'll put every cent back into your account.

499
00:33:35,835 --> 00:33:37,000
Ye,

500
00:33:37,000 --> 00:33:38,000
take this.

501
00:33:38,000 --> 00:33:41,560
When you have time,
go to the bank with Wu and take out the money.

502
00:33:42,319 --> 00:33:44,200
Grandma, you'll get

503
00:33:44,200 --> 00:33:45,905
three times this amount back.

504
00:33:45,905 --> 00:33:46,920
Okay,

505
00:33:46,920 --> 00:33:49,465
then I'll wait to live off the interest.

506
00:33:50,319 --> 00:33:51,360
Are you sure there's only

507
00:33:51,360 --> 00:33:52,559
300 yuan in this account?

508
00:33:52,559 --> 00:33:54,039
I'm sure.

509
00:33:54,039 --> 00:33:55,080
But my grandma said

510
00:33:55,080 --> 00:33:56,319
there was 10,000 yuan in it.

511
00:33:56,319 --> 00:33:57,880
- Yeah.
- Please wait a moment.

512
00:33:57,880 --> 00:34:00,000
Let me print a balance statement for you.

513
00:34:00,640 --> 00:34:02,640
Here you go.

514
00:34:05,559 --> 00:34:07,720
356 yuan.

515
00:34:07,720 --> 00:34:08,840
Maybe...

516
00:34:08,840 --> 00:34:11,159
Could Grandma have remembered it wrong?

517
00:34:11,159 --> 00:34:13,199
Can you check the transaction records?

518
00:34:13,199 --> 00:34:14,920
Sure, please wait.

519
00:34:18,000 --> 00:34:20,240
There was indeed a deposit of over 10,000 yuan.

520
00:34:20,240 --> 00:34:22,800
But it was taken out two years ago.

521
00:34:26,800 --> 00:34:28,360
Thank you.

522
00:34:31,119 --> 00:34:32,880
Xing Wu, do you know

523
00:34:32,880 --> 00:34:34,519
who took it out?

524
00:34:34,519 --> 00:34:35,840
Xing Guo Dong.

525
00:34:35,840 --> 00:34:37,440
Your dad.

526
00:34:38,519 --> 00:34:39,960
So that's why he came back suddenly

527
00:34:39,960 --> 00:34:41,159
to take Grandma's ID card.

528
00:34:41,159 --> 00:34:43,239
He even had her sign some kind of consent form.

529
00:34:43,239 --> 00:34:44,290
Did he have

530
00:34:44,290 --> 00:34:45,519
gambling debts?

531
00:34:45,519 --> 00:34:47,519
He must have taken the money to pay them off.

532
00:34:47,519 --> 00:34:49,079
He had a pile of debts,

533
00:34:49,079 --> 00:34:51,239
and still dared to take Grandma's savings.

534
00:34:51,239 --> 00:34:53,240
So where is he now?

535
00:34:53,840 --> 00:34:55,480
He's dead.

536
00:35:11,559 --> 00:35:13,400
Fang.

537
00:35:13,400 --> 00:35:15,170
There are scissors and stuff in this box.

538
00:35:15,170 --> 00:35:16,197
Can they still be used?

539
00:35:16,197 --> 00:35:17,280
Keep them for me.

540
00:35:17,280 --> 00:35:19,080
Okay, okay.

541
00:35:20,440 --> 00:35:21,960
Fang.

542
00:35:22,614 --> 00:35:24,280
- Liu Nian, what...
- Fang.

543
00:35:24,280 --> 00:35:27,119
As soon as I heard the news, I rushed back.

544
00:35:27,119 --> 00:35:28,400
I didn't think

545
00:35:28,400 --> 00:35:30,095
it would be this bad.

546
00:35:32,519 --> 00:35:35,079
We were talking about expanding before,

547
00:35:35,079 --> 00:35:36,239
but now,

548
00:35:36,239 --> 00:35:37,880
before we even got started,

549
00:35:37,880 --> 00:35:39,199
you've lost your job.

550
00:35:39,199 --> 00:35:40,400
It's okay, Fang.

551
00:35:40,400 --> 00:35:41,440
If you want me,

552
00:35:41,440 --> 00:35:43,400
I'll stay and work for you. Look.

553
00:35:43,400 --> 00:35:45,159
I even brought my luggage.

554
00:35:45,159 --> 00:35:47,080
There's nothing for you here.

555
00:35:47,080 --> 00:35:50,079
You should go find a job right now.

556
00:35:50,079 --> 00:35:52,320
Otherwise,
how will you take care of your grandma?

557
00:35:52,320 --> 00:35:54,599
How will you all survive?

558
00:35:54,599 --> 00:35:56,712
But Fang, this is when you need help the most.

559
00:35:56,712 --> 00:35:57,760
I have to be here.

560
00:35:57,760 --> 00:35:59,239
Otherwise, I'd feel guilty.

561
00:35:59,239 --> 00:36:01,360
If you stay here, then I'll feel guilty.

562
00:36:01,360 --> 00:36:03,520
I've got nothing to give you.

563
00:36:04,754 --> 00:36:06,078
Just do as I say.

564
00:36:06,078 --> 00:36:07,559
Find a decent job.

565
00:36:07,559 --> 00:36:10,400
Just work hard and make a living.

566
00:36:13,159 --> 00:36:15,280
Okay, Fang, I'll listen to you.

567
00:36:15,280 --> 00:36:17,719
If you need anything, call me.

568
00:36:17,719 --> 00:36:19,079
I'll come right away.

569
00:36:19,079 --> 00:36:21,760
I'll check what else you can still use.

570
00:36:21,760 --> 00:36:23,320
Liu Nian.

571
00:36:50,171 --> 00:36:51,800
- Auntie.
- Mom.

572
00:36:51,800 --> 00:36:52,972
You're back.

573
00:36:52,972 --> 00:36:54,000
How did it go?

574
00:36:54,000 --> 00:36:55,760
Did you get the money?

575
00:36:57,639 --> 00:36:58,679
What's wrong?

576
00:36:58,679 --> 00:37:01,399
Grandma's savings are gone.

577
00:37:01,399 --> 00:37:02,599
Gone?

578
00:37:02,599 --> 00:37:04,880
They've been gone for years.

579
00:37:04,880 --> 00:37:06,960
Xing Guo Dong took them.

580
00:37:08,719 --> 00:37:10,360
How can you be sure it was him?

581
00:37:10,360 --> 00:37:12,159
The bank has records.

582
00:37:12,159 --> 00:37:14,920
The dates and details all match up.

583
00:37:15,559 --> 00:37:16,800
Aside from him,

584
00:37:16,800 --> 00:37:19,040
it couldn't have been anyone else.

585
00:37:25,709 --> 00:37:28,760
Don't tell Grandma about this yet.

586
00:37:28,760 --> 00:37:30,026
Find some coupons

587
00:37:30,026 --> 00:37:31,920
and put them in an envelope.

588
00:37:31,920 --> 00:37:34,440
Tell Grandma we got the money.

589
00:37:37,760 --> 00:37:38,800
Let's clean up.

590
00:37:38,800 --> 00:37:40,320
Don't worry.

591
00:37:54,679 --> 00:37:57,360
The food is really good today.

592
00:37:57,360 --> 00:38:00,760
So, you've got to spend money when it's needed.

593
00:38:04,079 --> 00:38:05,920
Grandma is right.

594
00:38:05,920 --> 00:38:07,240
We've already got enough

595
00:38:07,240 --> 00:38:08,840
to cover our daily expenses for now.

596
00:38:08,840 --> 00:38:10,320
We don't have to worry about money.

597
00:38:10,320 --> 00:38:11,519
That's right, Mom.

598
00:38:11,519 --> 00:38:13,459
They have already given me the money.

599
00:38:13,459 --> 00:38:15,840
I've got it. Don't worry.

600
00:38:15,840 --> 00:38:17,134
Ye and Wu

601
00:38:17,134 --> 00:38:18,880
are under a lot of pressure with school.

602
00:38:18,880 --> 00:38:20,679
They need to eat well.

603
00:38:20,679 --> 00:38:21,920
Here. Come on, eat more.

604
00:38:21,920 --> 00:38:23,440
Mom, I'll get you some more fish soup.

605
00:38:23,440 --> 00:38:25,719
- Okay.
- This fish is really fresh.

606
00:38:25,719 --> 00:38:27,280
It's good.

607
00:38:28,679 --> 00:38:30,000
It's a whole fish.

608
00:38:30,000 --> 00:38:31,000
Yes.

609
00:38:31,000 --> 00:38:33,240
Yeah. It's best with tofu.

610
00:38:33,240 --> 00:38:35,280
- It's more nutritious.
- Here.

611
00:38:35,280 --> 00:38:37,146
Thank you.

612
00:40:37,203 --> 00:40:38,920
Boss, let me explain.

613
00:40:38,920 --> 00:40:41,519
I never meant to hide anything.

614
00:40:41,519 --> 00:40:43,484
It's really not what you think.

615
00:40:43,484 --> 00:40:45,400
Boss, please listen to me.

616
00:40:45,400 --> 00:40:46,760
What's there to explain?

617
00:40:46,760 --> 00:40:48,400
You hid something this big from us.

618
00:40:48,400 --> 00:40:49,800
I didn't hide it.

619
00:40:49,800 --> 00:40:51,840
They didn't ask when they hired me.

620
00:40:51,840 --> 00:40:53,039
Well, I'm asking now.

621
00:40:53,039 --> 00:40:54,464
We don't hire people with a record.

622
00:40:54,464 --> 00:40:56,519
- Now leave.
- Boss...

623
00:40:56,519 --> 00:40:59,360
Then... how about my wages?

624
00:40:59,360 --> 00:41:01,760
Don't worry. I won't short you a single cent.

625
00:41:01,760 --> 00:41:03,760
I'll send it to you via WeChat now.

626
00:41:03,760 --> 00:41:06,505
I've been working since this morning.

627
00:41:06,505 --> 00:41:07,640
They're about to serve lunch.

628
00:41:07,640 --> 00:41:10,199
Can I get a boxed lunch?

629
00:41:10,199 --> 00:41:11,931
- Eat and then leave quickly.
- Okay.

630
00:41:37,639 --> 00:41:39,280
Drink some water.

631
00:41:56,239 --> 00:41:57,559
So tell me.

632
00:41:57,559 --> 00:41:59,400
What was that all about?

633
00:42:01,280 --> 00:42:03,239
What else could it be?

634
00:42:03,239 --> 00:42:04,880
I got fired.

635
00:42:04,880 --> 00:42:07,440
Because I've been to prison. I have a record.

636
00:42:16,519 --> 00:42:17,880
What's this?

637
00:42:17,880 --> 00:42:19,480
A job.

638
00:42:24,416 --> 00:42:26,039
I don't know anything about raising fish.

639
00:42:26,039 --> 00:42:27,280
Besides,

640
00:42:27,280 --> 00:42:28,880
who would dare

641
00:42:28,880 --> 00:42:30,560
hire someone like me?

642
00:42:32,559 --> 00:42:34,107
Don't worry.

643
00:42:34,107 --> 00:42:37,159
This is your sister's friend's fish farm.

644
00:42:37,159 --> 00:42:39,640
I've already talked to the boss.

645
00:42:41,220 --> 00:42:42,360
It's up to you whether you go.

646
00:42:42,360 --> 00:42:43,920
I'll leave it here.

647
00:43:14,800 --> 00:43:15,800
Hello, Uncle Sun.

648
00:43:15,800 --> 00:43:16,962
Happy New Year.

649
00:43:16,962 --> 00:43:18,000
<i>Ye.</i>

650
00:43:18,000 --> 00:43:19,685
<i>Happy New Year.</i>

651
00:43:19,685 --> 00:43:22,021
- I wanted to...
<i>- Wait a moment.</i>

652
00:43:22,021 --> 00:43:23,280
Okay.

653
00:43:23,280 --> 00:43:25,719
<i>Number 101, please.
Window three for your medicine.</i>

654
00:43:25,719 --> 00:43:27,433
<i>That's me. Thank you.</i>

655
00:43:27,433 --> 00:43:29,679
<i>Go ahead, Ye.</i>

656
00:43:29,679 --> 00:43:31,199
Wait, Uncle Sun, what's wrong?

657
00:43:31,199 --> 00:43:33,199
Why are you at the hospital?

658
00:43:33,199 --> 00:43:34,519
<i>I'm fine.</i>

659
00:43:34,519 --> 00:43:36,559
<i>My mother-in-law just had an operation.</i>

660
00:43:36,559 --> 00:43:38,539
<i>I'm picking up her medicine.</i>

